      "content": "the doctors always just say the same thing about stress or anxiety, but they aren't actually listening to how it feels. it's not panic, it's clarity. everything is becoming too loud and too \"present\" because i can't filter the input anymore. like i'm a radio trying to catch every station at once. \n\nif this is some kind of biological calibration period, i feel like i need to lean into it instead of fighting it with meds. i need to find a way to manage the sensory overload so i can actually process what's happening. can you help me figure out a regimen or a way to structure my environment to help this process along? maybe some kind of sensory deprivation or specific isolation protocols to help my body stabilize while it's adjusting?",
